+# Tablet loading phase profiling — 2026-11-07
+
+**TPP01/TPP02/TPPQ01: Physical-tablet profiling complete; normal app restored.** Six accepted runs pass **280 checks / zero failures**, covering startup, two full menu tours, 24 unscored race loads and 24 same-Game retries. This is measurement and source review, not a delivered 50% loading improvement. No shipping game source or backend code is changed by this task.
+
+The highest-value finding is specific to the current saved setup: **the fitted Compact with simple car models enabled cannot use either prepared live-car restoration path**. Every race entry rebuilds it procedurally. Across the 12 repeat entries, that stage takes **2.247–2.691 seconds**, median **2.468 seconds**, and a median **67.8%** of race-ready time. Across all 24 entries it yields **108–136 times**. This is wall time including cooperative frame waits, not pure CPU time. Supporting exact prepared simple fitted cars, or a validated bounded live rest-pose cache for this configuration, is the strongest next target for halving repeat race loads.
+
+The normal app `0.3.0-creator.e14bec0e820302b39bbb8c16684bda60` is restored byte-exact at APK level, with the original first-install timestamp. All **22 checked authored-track JSON files** and **both PB dictionaries** remain unchanged. The normal signed-in Rivalry screen was inspected in a private native screenshot and actual foreground activity was verified. Ordinary cache/session refreshes change some files: there were **802 files before** and **814 afterward**, so this report does not claim all app files are byte-identical after launches. Android's original stay-awake setting remains **0**. No uninstall, clear-data, canonical race completion or score submission occurred.
+
+**Device and controls.** OnePlus Pad 2 / OPD2403, Android 15, Adreno 750, ARM64, official Godot 4.7.2, Compatibility renderer. The saved car, fitted parts and graphics preferences are copied privately into diagnostic race records. Existing app/driver caches remain. Each accepted run starts a new process; each race run visits Pine, Winter, Desert, Night and Storm in that fixed order, twice each, then Star/Pine twice. The diagnostic road/layout directory starts empty for run A and persists into run B; process-local world caches start again with each process. These are serial cache-state observations, not virgin-driver, randomized A/B, all-car or online-admission benchmarks. Battery temperature is **27.1–27.5°C** across the six accepted runs; reported Android thermal status is **0** throughout. No sustained driving, memory/PSS or GPU-frequency qualification is claimed.
+
+Two normal-client controls reach `APP_READY` in **3.426 / 3.496 seconds**. Two final-profiler launches with the marker absent take **3.406 / 3.509 seconds**. Their medians differ by about 3 ms, below the approximately 50 ms host/device clock-calibration uncertainty. This does not establish zero observer cost; it finds no resolved startup regression in these small controls. Accepted active observations require the actual intended menu rather than the transient restoring view. Network timings include route/callback/main-thread scheduling waits; decode/encode timings can include worker waits. They are not pure server latency or CPU samples.
+
+**Startup.** The two dedicated samples reach fully presented Rivalry content at **6.888 / 6.663 seconds** from the launch request, although `APP_READY` fires at **3.478 / 3.448 seconds**. All six initial-menu observations span **6.663–7.560 seconds**. The dedicated samples have a **1.950 / 1.962-second** main-loop gap before initial content readiness and a further **1.129 / 1.108-second** gap in the following idle observation. The nominal three-second idle wait itself stretches under that work. Initial readiness therefore needs both a content milestone and an assessment of work continuing immediately afterward.
+
+Rivalry's first synchronous feature-resource load is about **0.77–0.78 seconds** in the dedicated samples. Account restoration as a whole is about **0.89–0.91 seconds** there. The large remaining frame gaps include construction/render/background work; the last event label is only a temporal neighbour. This trace does not attribute the entire gap to a specific network response or shader compiler. Split the large live-view preparation and attribute the post-ready background stall before choosing a native shader or engine change.
+
+The existing **menu snapshot writer is broken on the tablet**. The unmodified normal APK logs a busy-parent `add_child()` failure from `menu_snapshot_writer.gd:25` during App readiness. Every accepted run ends with the writer outside the scene tree, **three pending paths / zero completed writes**. RAM snapshots can still be present, but these pending snapshots are not being persisted by this writer. Correct its root attachment lifecycle and preserve processing of values queued before `_ready`; simply deferring attachment while retaining `_ready`'s unconditional `set_process(false)` could still strand queued data. Preserve account/origin/day/week guards and atomic writing. A before/after restart benchmark remains necessary to quantify the loading benefit.
+
+**Menus.** Each cell is the median of two visits in the corresponding cycle. Timings include the normal page transition, applicable asynchronous content readiness and final draw fences. The first measured Rivalry visit follows initial startup Rivalry; it is an explicit re-entry, not the first-ever appearance.
+
+| Menu | First visit, median seconds | Repeat, median seconds |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Biome | 0.398 | 0.409 |
+| Challenges | 0.377 | 0.226 |
+| Editor | 2.049 | 1.564 |
+| Daily | 0.750 | 0.555 |
+| Drafts | 0.517 | 0.208 |
+| Garage | 1.454 | 0.423 |
+| Profile | 0.160 | 0.106 |
+| Rivalry | 1.302 | 0.257 |
+| Settings | 0.220 | 0.119 |
+| Store | 0.386 | 0.351 |
+| Tracks | 0.162 | 0.141 |
+
+All four Daily visits have data available and no card failure. Both Garage cycles in each run assert direct entry without a modal feature-loading window and retain both reflection views. Editor visits use a private new-draft library, wait for the actual prepared native preview and completed worker/commit state, then restore the original library/document. Editor and initial Garage/Rivalry entries deserve attention before the already short Profile/Settings/Tracks entries. Scene/resource reuse must remain bounded by the existing mobile memory policy; a different reuse strategy needs complete-journey measurement as well as a single-menu timing. The earlier rejected podium-picture cache remains rejected; its Garage tradeoff is documented in the previous loading pass.
+
+**Local race preparation.** These are `_start_race` to prepared Game times. Fixture compilation is measured separately: oval **0.113–0.273 seconds**, Star **0.285–0.366 seconds**. Ordinary selected-track preparation can happen before a race tap; these compilation observations must not be silently folded into or subtracted from a different whole-loading definition. The production Game retains five laps and countdown360 and is frozen at tick zero before another yield. Cloud tickets, rating/ad preparation, race telemetry and owner last-track persistence are excluded; normal menu/startup reads remain. Results therefore exclude competitive admission, Daily limits and ticket network latency.
+
+| Local fixture/theme | Run A first entry, s | Run B first entry, s | Repeat entries, range s |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| oval/pine | 13.044 | 12.359 | 3.195–3.286 |
+| oval/winter | 5.604 | 5.479 | 3.322–3.381 |
+| oval/desert | 9.338 | 8.088 | 3.880–3.956 |
+| oval/night_city | 13.071 | 7.074 | 3.508–3.704 |
+| oval/storm | 9.959 | 5.850 | 3.562–3.575 |
+| star/pine | 20.906 | 11.280 | 3.496–3.708 |
+
+Same-Game retry is already **16–34 ms**, with the original full countdown and tick-zero invariants retained. The repeat-load bottleneck is creating a new Game/car, not this retry path.
+
+The first Star/Pine run spends **5.440 seconds in road preparation**, then **14.597 seconds in Game preparation**, which includes the **2.254-second car stage**. On the fresh process with the diagnostic disk cache retained, its road phase is **0.184 seconds**, but Game preparation remains **9.860 seconds**, including a **2.521-second car stage**. Its visible native world-preparation phase is only **0.081 / 0.490 seconds** in those two entries. Track compilation/checkpoint layout is not the dominant Star cost here; final world/scenery construction and car work are the next targets. Use final validated scenery artifacts or exact retained prepared scenes, with bounded memory and complete geometry/version/source validation; do not expand the existing checkpoint artifact and claim it solves the measured world cost.
+
+Night's first explicit native graphics preparation is **4.693 seconds in run A / 0.524 seconds in run B**; effects preparation is **2.400 / 0.993 seconds**. Storm's graphics phase is **3.820 / 0.479 seconds**. Existing caches clearly matter, but these serial observations cannot isolate driver caching from all other cache-state differences. Keep exact settings/material/light/source contexts and original fallback compilation in any selective native-preparation work. The separately built custom Android engine remains unqualified and was not installed for this task. Broad shader-source splitting and a renderer switch have not been demonstrated to improve this tablet's complete loading journey.
+
+**Why the car rebuilds.** `CarVisual._restore_modular_model()` explicitly returns false for fitted simple models because their original shadow/caster geometry is not yet covered by the prepared route. `PreparedCarCache.restore()` also excludes simple models and only accepts the proven stock detailed Compact. The current saved Compact has non-stock aero/body/hood/rims and simple models enabled. Thus valid general prepared assets do not make this particular runtime path eligible. The observed nonzero model-yield counts and snapshot-stage construction agree with that source path. The safe alternative is to prepare and verify this exact combination, including moving parts, shadows, livery and independent mutable materials. Raising the four-millisecond cooperative budget alone may shorten wall time while worsening visible frame stalls, and it does not remove the work. Do not remove an appearance guard to make a timing green. See the sanitized [rendering context and source hashes](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/rendering-context.json).
+
+**Recommended order.** First qualify prepared/reusable simple fitted car geometry, because it addresses the largest repeat-entry cost. In parallel with a later implementation pass, correct the snapshot writer's lifecycle and quantify restart behavior. Then address Star's final world/scenery construction and reduce/attribute startup's large live-menu and post-ready stalls. Editor preparation and the remaining first-use Night/Storm native paths follow. Validate each change against the same settings, first/repeat/process-restart cases and complete menu→Garage→race journey; retain exact appearance/canonical checks. The universal **50% target is still unproven**. For the measured repeat entries, the approximately 2.47-second car stage is a concrete opportunity, not a promised saving.
+
+**Implementation and validation.** Five production files are instrumented only in the private source copy: `core/app.gd`, `backend/account_controller.gd`, `backend/backend_client.gd`, `core/features/race.gd`, `ui/garage_preloader.gd`. Three task-owned diagnostic scripts implement bounded events, the observer and embedded existing fixtures. Render/shader/car/road builders remain unchanged. The five build identities for checkpoint layout, Garage, per-car Garage, modular cars and header pictures match the exact normal snapshot, preventing observer-induced visual-cache invalidation. The final profiler APK is **320496512 bytes**, **8879 ZIP entries**, all CRCs valid, ARM64 only; native libraries are byte-exact to the normal APK. SHA-256: `986df4e4c266650193af65c85ef9e31b1bcd725aea3b2e38e264de6f7857a29a`. Build: `0.3.0-creator.5461f09de97da8ac7b795c7d097e3912`.
+
+The pinned standard `scripts/dev.ps1 -Action ExportAndroid -AndroidPreset "Android ARM64" -QuickValidation -CommandTimeoutSeconds 600` passes import/startup, prepared468/1925checks, five-picture provenance, driving72/0, catalogue21/0 and menus41/0. The final export takes **321.406 seconds**; its source audit changes only generated `build_identity.gd` / `project.godot`. The final private desktop navigation control passes **2/0** without source changes. Earlier observer QA includes stable headless19/0, native race19/0 and native Editor5/0; these desktop durations are not tablet evidence. The six accepted actual-tablet runs pass startup2+2, menus28+28 and races110+110, with no dropped trace events. Canonical simulation is not modified. This is not a full regression/physics merge gate.
+
+Commands actually run include `prepare.py`, private `run_export.py`, `check_probe.py`, `run_device.py install`, `run_device.py measure`, `run_device.py restore`, `analyse.py`, `package_receipt.py` and this report writer. ADB uses replace-install and the task's explicit local marker; no data clearing. The normal restoration launches successfully at about **3.464 seconds to APP_READY**, then its native signed-in menu and actual activity are checked separately. The first `dumpsys window windows` probe omitted the focus field and falsely recorded false; full window/activity queries and the inspected screenshot verify the restored foreground state. The private screenshot remains under ignored build storage.
+
+**Retained failures and limits.** Installed-source identity checks catch two unrelated newer deployments during preparation; neither stale profiling client is installed over them. The exact latest source is rebased and its original APK/data backed up. Secure-lock pauses require the owner's unlock; a global stay-awake write is rejected by Android and makes no change. Initial isolation misses `.gitattributes` / `godot-version.txt`, then recovers in the owned copy. One desktop QA overlaps export identity generation and is not a stable-source acceptance; the subsequent stable control passes. Initial private Editor fixtures lack owner metadata and fail real native readiness, then pass after inheriting the library owner field. Existing parent-busy, desktop certificate-store/teardown, catalogue-anchor and embedded-text export warnings remain; this report does not claim clean engine logs.
+
+The initial tablet observer incorrectly accepts the transient restoring screen. Its two startup runs and associated menu receipts are explicitly archived as **rejected readiness evidence**, not included in the accepted summary. The corrected observer waits for restored navigation and validates actual page content, and both host collection and analysis independently reject restoring-screen results. Android console truncates long JSON phase rows, so final analysis uses complete on-device JSON files instead of parsing those lines. A live progress-row parsing attempt fails for this reason and does not modify the run. Initial source/anchor/path failures and all build attempts remain under the task build folder. No shipping fix, backend deployment/admin operation, custom engine or persistent lock-policy change is delivered by this profiling task. Normal app network behavior continues to refresh its usual data.
+
+[Accepted summary](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/summary.json), [method](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/METHOD.md), [package proof](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/package.json), [restoration](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/restoration.json), [source overlay](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/instrumentation.json), and [reversible task-only checkpoint](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/checkpoint.json). Private APKs, account files, exact file manifests, draft/preference copies and full logs remain only in ignored build storage. No main-index staging, commit or reset is performed.
+
+The final [source comparison](evidence/tablet-phase-profile-2026-11-07/source-proof.json) checks 1965 baseline and 1968 profiling source/resource declarations outside asset/imported/Android-generated directories. Its differences are exactly the five declared instruments, two generated metadata files and three diagnostic scripts. The initial-copy manifest is retained under superseded evidence. The review patch preserves original terminal blank lines in archived source preimages; its initial EOF whitespace rejection is retained, and the final check excludes only that archive EOF rule while retaining trailing-space/tab checks and byte-exact forward/reverse validation.
